agm: 1.0
package: agent.memory
version: 0.1.0
title: Agent Memory System

node agent.memory.session_entry
type: entity
summary: represents a persisted memory entry scoped to an agent session
priority: normal
stability: medium
fields:
  - id: uuid
  - session_id: uuid
  - agent_id: string
  - content: string
  - content_type: enum[fact, decision, observation, task_result]
  - tags: list[string]
  - created_at: timestamp
  - expires_at: timestamp
  - confidence: float
  - source_node_id: string
detail:
  A memory entry captures something an agent observed, decided, or produced
  during a session. Entries are tagged for retrieval and optionally expire.
  Confidence scores allow agents to weight conflicting memories.

  content_type semantics:
    fact: asserted truth about the world or codebase
    decision: a choice made and its rationale
    observation: a measurement or sampled state
    task_result: the output of a completed task
notes: Memory entries are vector-indexed for semantic search alongside keyword index.
